HTTrack 3.50, the first Android release in nine years.

• HTTPS works again: the 2017 build's TLS is too old for most sites
• Runs on current Android, and is 64-bit
• Modern pages are captured, including srcset and lazy-loaded images
• Mirrors go to shared storage, so other apps can open them
• Updating a mirror no longer deletes files it should keep
• Options do what they say, and the finish screen says what happened

Report problems on GitHub.